    "question": {
      ":question/id": "55907a7c-d0cf-5bfa-a564-b7492ad55be4",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x-150^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter exact coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\sin(x-150^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-150^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 150^\\circ-\\cos x\\sin 150^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe plus sign outside the second blank is supplied. The entries are $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $-\\frac{1}{2}$, respectively.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "df1b8751-7857-56c8-a7f9-2ce5251064c4",
